ere comes wanda vision now this is just  a cover photo but we do have  six new images from actual episodes of  the series and we'll start off with this  first one which is kind of  odd but most of the show seems like it  is going to be rather odd which is  awesome  but it's of wanda and vision and as we  can see here they are sleeping  in separated beds now this is kind of  done for two reasons one  is that with the old sitcoms it was  actually illegal to show them  sleeping in the same bed it was illegal  for them to show that on tv  now this kind of just further adds to  the weirdness of their relationship but  if you look at wanda she's looking a  little bit confused now we know this is  going to involve  different realities so it's almost like  wanda just woke up  and was randomly in this room with  vision it's either that or she has  noticed something weird or she has heard  something and it doesn't all make sense  and if you take a look at the shadows on  the wall between the beds of wanda and  vision we can see a shadow that kind of  looks like a witch's hat now of course  this is just a shadow from the bedpost  but this is also most likely a reference  to  witchcraft we know agatha harkness is  involved and we know that there's going  to be witchcraft in the show  and for those who might think this is  digging a little bit too deep marvel has  actually already done this with their  first promotional art for the one  division series if we take a look at the  two of them sitting on the couch holding  hands if you look in the upper left hand  corner you can see both of their shadows  and while wanda and vision are sitting  on the couch in human form you can see  in the upper left-hand corner their  shadows are of their superhero forms we  can see vision as an android and we can  see the scarlet witch in her full  scarlet witch costume and speaking of  witches the next photo is of catherine  han's mysterious character  called agnes now again it's pretty much  confirmed that she  is in fact agatha harkness after all  agnes is just agatha  and harkness combined to make one word  but she'll also be playing the unusual  nosy neighbor and in this photo it looks  like she came over to give the couple a  pineapple or to borrow one either way  it's kind of weird  now the next photo is actually a very  important photo it's of wanda  pregnant now the important part of this  photo is one not only does it confirm  that wanda is going to be pregnant and  will indeed have kids which  has already been confirmed but the  second part is look at their faces they  both look to be an extreme confusement  and this is most likely because  wanda is going to randomly get pregnant  in the comics it happens out of nowhere  vision doesn't  actually give wand a kid she just  becomes pregnant and that is especially  true if you consider the fact that  they're sleeping in separate beds in the  show but they do look  very confused in this scene and vision  is reaching out to touch her stomach  almost like i can't believe it how did  this even happen  this almost definitely confirms that  mephisto is going to be in the one  division series and he is the one  responsible for wanda getting pregnant  this is a page right out of the comics  where wanda gets impregnated by magic  and we would go on to find that her two  children are actually the shards of the  demon mephisto  and ultimately he would take them back  and her children would be gone and this  is what eventually led to her kind of  losing her mind  and creating the house of m reality  where magneto ruled the world  now the rest of the photos are kind of  just fun photos there's one envision  leading over the kitchen counter  looking at each other smiling you can  tell that they're really happy there's  wanda envision inside the kitchen again  and wanda has a weird expression on her  face  perhaps performing some type of magic  and then the last one with a  very confused look on her face and she  is indeed performing magic using her  powers to cook  it looks like she's preparing dinner and  something really ticked her off or  surprised her  now there's a lot of commentary about  the show that gives us some pretty big  reveal so let's break it down  for starters it has been confirmed that  the first episode of the wanna vision  series was in fact filmed in front of a  live  audience something that marvel studios  has never done before  now to start it off we actually get kind  of a little synopsis about the show  and the synopsis reads as follows set  after end game the series starts with  the married witch  and android living in the idyllic town  of west view  we find wanda envision living a blissful  suburban existence  trying to keep their powers under wraps  but as the newly weds cycle through the  decades and the familiar tv tropes they  realize their white picket fence life  may not be as gleamingly picture perfect  as it seems  now you have to remember that with the  first teaser that we got for the one  division series they most likely just  showed us the first episode or first  couple of episodes we know and it's  confirmed right here that the one  division series is going to go through  the decades  very very quickly tayonna paris who is  going to be playing monica rambo said  that this is going to be an  action-packed tv series and we know  we're really not going to get that in  these tv sitcom type of eras so we're  going to go through and get out of these  sitcom eras pretty quickly as they said  as they cycle through the decades that  means their kids are going to grow up  very fast as well now another huge thing  that has been revealed by this article  that has been speculated for a very long  time is that we are going to see wanda  fully explore the scarlet witch and the  scarlet witch's powers  she has yet to be called the scarlet  witch and it has been confirmed they are  going to indeed call her that in this  series at one point  and she has yet to discover her full  powers but that is going to change in  this series  the article says one division promised a  chance to explore wanda's past and the  full  capabilities of her telekinetic powers  in initial conversations about the show  feige won her over by referencing  specific scarlet witch  comic story lines although she won't  reveal which ones  due to spoilers then it quotes elizabeth  olsen saying it's been the biggest gift  that marvel's given me getting to do  this show  you get to just focus on her and not how  she felt through everyone else's story  lines so it's all about wanda and the  scarlet witch and although they say they  can't reference the comic book  storylines we pretty much know that a  good chunk of the tv series is going to  be based off of the house of  m storyline and i actually did a video  not too long ago  explaining all the comics that one  division is going to be based off of and  i'll link that down below and put it up  above  but the great news is we're going to see  the scarlet witch and her  full powers in this show now mary  lovanos who is a co-producer of the show  says it's really incredible to be able  to tell a long form story  the way the comics did in a sense a tv  show is a multiple  issue comic book run which is something  that from the marvel development side we  totally do  understand so this is really really cool  because in a way we're going to get a  more  comic like tv show than we've ever  gotten before and it was explained in  this ew  article that this is very different from  the netflix marvel shows and  agents of shield because kevin feige had  complete creative control over these  series so this  is full mcu these are basically going to  be movies packed into one hour long  episodes in fact tayonna paris who is  playing monica rambo says  i was like oh i thought we were doing a  little show but no it's six  marvel movies packed into what they're  presenting as a sitcom  so disney plus really is giving us  marvel fans a very  unique and awesome opportunity instead  of just getting one two hour film we're  getting  six one hour episodes that's going to be  like six different movies packed into  one season  and hopefully there will be multiple  seasons and to top it all off  ew says in their article ideally marvel  hopes  one division will be just the pilot  episode of a long-running tv dynasty  the studio is already hard at work  developing seven additional shows  with each one connecting to past and  future films  one division kevin feige notes will  directly set up the 2022 film  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness with olson's witch  playing a key role alongside benedict  cumberbatch as sorcerer  and notice how they specifically said  elizabeth olsen's  witch that means by the end of the one  division series leading right up to  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness she is going to be  a fool scarlet witch with her full  powers so we are definitely  in for a treat with the one division  series it sounds like it's going to be  absolutely insane which i love  and it sounds like wanda is definitely  going to become one of the most  strongest characters in the entire  marvel cinematic universe if she wasn't  already  so let me know what you think about all  these reveals from this ew article  and also of the new photos that we got  as well let me know in the comments what  you're most excited about for the  wanavision series  don't forget to subscribe so you can  stay up to date on all of the latest  marvel news  give the video a like if you enjoyed it  and for live updates you can follow me  on instagram and twitter  as always thank you all so much for  watching woof

